Third-party configuration
-------------------------
These navigation configuration files follow upstream example configurations.
Parameter names, structure and some default values come from those projects;
RobotOps selects and tunes the values for its robot and worlds.

  ros2_ws/src/robot_navigation/config/navigation.yaml
  ros2_ws/src/robot_navigation/config/localization.yaml
  ros2_ws/src/robot_navigation/config/profiles/navfn_rpp.yaml
  ros2_ws/src/robot_navigation/config/profiles/smac_dwb.yaml
    Based on Nav2 nav2_bringup/params/nav2_params.yaml. The DWB critic block in
    smac_dwb.yaml is adapted from that file.
    Nav2 (navigation2), Apache License 2.0
    https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2

  ros2_ws/src/robot_navigation/config/slam.yaml
    Parameter names follow SLAM Toolbox config/mapper_params_online_async.yaml.
    SLAM Toolbox, GNU LGPL 2.1
    https://github.com/SteveMacenski/slam_toolbox

Dependencies
------------
RobotOps builds against, but does not include, ROS 2, Nav2, SLAM Toolbox,
Gazebo, ros2_control and npm/PyPI packages. Their own licenses apply. The
robot_navigation slam_runner links SLAM Toolbox (LGPL); review LGPL obligations
before distributing compiled binaries or container images.

